{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/52935-share-your-signature-character","id":52935,"title":"Share your Signature character!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-18T19:27:37-08:00","id":52935,"title":"Share your Signature character!","content":"Everyone has a signature character on different games, A Character you grew fond with and that you even use as an NPC on your games. Lets share them!.<br /> <br /> Werewolf the apocalypse:<br /> Joe Torienark: AKA: Laughing Bastard. Nuwisha<br /> His Grandpa is Old Man Manyskins. Age : 22, The Havok wearing Poncho, Learned all the tricks o' the trade thanks to his grandpa, touring USA to bring some &quot;Fun.&quot; to Pentex, usually finding himself in the middle of the crossfire, His job (as the ST who has faced this char) is usually to bring new players to caerns and explain them the basic rules of the WtA Mythos, He is a very calculative guy even if he is always smiling and laughing, very cartoony guy.<br /> Fetishes: Big Breasted G- Oh.. you mean artifacts... The Poncho of Moncho: level 3 relic which allows him to pass as a &quot;Metis.&quot; (explaining his size...not That size you perv....this is getting awkward). The Cane o' Wind: LVL 2 fetish basically a long cane he uses to walk which allows him to do &quot;Cutting Wind.&quot; well, not very cuting but it helps to raise sand and stuff like that.<br /> And last but not least: The Alpha Omega Pack or Acme Pack of Wibbily Wobbily, a level 5 fetish, this is basically a small bag he carries to his side, in which he can Materialize Random objecs (the ST determines what comes out and a rol of 'Choose pair or unpair' on a dice determines if its what he is looking for), It cant materialize things like REAL WEAPONS or silver, but theres mythos of how he ran away from a Wyrm Tainted spirit, All the way from a hill summoning a Shoping Cart and going down the hill 'Johnny Knoxville Style' And Survive to it. Basically, a random bag of randomness...<br /> <br /> Demon The Fallen:<br /> Thomas Vincent Crowley<br /> Alastor.<br /> Halaku, Faustican<br /> Real descendant of Aliester Crowley (Some belive he was possessed when a group of cultist tried to summon Alastor and this one possessed the recent deseased Tommy Crowley.), No One trully knows for how long he has been on earth (Thanks to my ST, hes been on earth ever since the 1950's), Currently passing as a LA TV Producer. <br /> His experience with the supernatural allowed him Two Things, A ) To Know a bit of everything B ) High charisma = Lots of Friends and people who owe him favors. Even if as Alastor, he is the Angel of Vengeance, he actually Loves mindkind and wishes them to Survive the Armageddon. Its Well documentated his Hatred for vampires and all Pentex related stuff, as well to have a sort of &quot;I wont fuck you, you wont fuck me.&quot; relation with werewolves (but its known that some parties of players have asked for his help whenever it comes to play in the cities or look for something specific within a city). His apocalyptic form includes Chains (tentacles), Claws (Hooks), Wings, Regeneration, Increaced iniciative, &quot;Rage&quot; (cant remember the name of that apocalyptic form which acts like the rage of a werewolf) among others. His current torment is 5 which he has keept in place for a while now but each day is harder... His highest lores are Death and Life oddly enough, He conciders himself a pacifist to certain degree, he wont fight unless provoked. Funny enough, as for the Infernal Court of L.A he acts as an outsider since his own personal ethics clash with everyone elses (He belives in redemption, he belives that everything was planned, he understands the power of faith, and he is looking for Uncle Lou. )<br /> <br /> Wraith The Oblivion. ( I havent finished this char so no Arcanos or guild yet, we just had his prelude)<br /> Joseph William Kerr<br /> Age:19<br /> Cause of Death: Violence<br /> A slacker.<br /> He quitted college, currently working on a convinance store. His girlfriend was a Rocker girl called Janet O'Byrne. Both lived happy togeather, His usual hangout was his local bar in which he spend time with his friends Ringo, Pat and the owner of the bar Noonan Which they saw him as a little brother and his boss Aaron Johansen. His family gave up on him time ago since never trully putting his time or efford in anything other than partying and spending time with Janet.<br /> His life spaned between playing with his NES, going to the Bar, His gf. <br /> His parents and family are Edgar Kerr: a Lawyer in boston and Elise Moore, the sort of woman who always has a glass of wine on her hand except when she does yoga, His older brother Eric (a medic), his little sister, Sarah (15 years old).<br /> He was forced into lawschool but he ran away from his family. Currently living in New Jersey.<br /> He was always a joker, a comedian.<br /> His Death: one night after closing the store, a group of muggers attacked him and drag him into an alley. His face was cut forcing a Glasglow smile on him, he fell into the ground while in shock, the group leader (4 muggers) decided it wasnt enough and he was shot multiple times around the chest and face (blowing off his left eye), As he felt on the ground, the leader thought it wasnt enough so, they poured alcohol on his hands and set them on fire... Later on he was found, he was taken to a hospital, spended 19 hours of suffering and agony.<br /> <br /> The Muggers Knew he was a comedian on the Bar, he was attacked because the leader of the gang thought he was making fun of him with a joke....Life is Fill with Irony.<br /> His fetters and passions consist on his barstool, his NES, and a ring he gave to Janet, his main goals are to let know to his friends that he is ok, and make sure Janet finds the right guy and for her to have the family he wasn't able to ever give her...as well a part of him wants revenge for being killed with out a proper reason and for being tortured.<br /> <br /> Share your signature characters <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T00:20:13-07:00","id":88005,"title":"","content":"Cage<br /> Vampire<br /> Generation 3rd (Embraced as 5th)<br /> Clan: True Brujah<br /> Flaws: Hunted, Amnesia<br /> Story: Woke up in the back of a hay wagon, and got involved with some neonates. Became a Prince in Romania, heavily involved in the scientific field for his time, specialized in the Occult. Had a giant magic chest of thousands of scrolls that had majority of lost information in it. Belonged to his Sire, who he didn't remember. Later got attacked by a hunter who he spared. This hunter would go on to be the Antediluvian of a new clan of Vampire call the Deo and their new Discipline, Manos Dio, which was reverse Daimonion that used Angel powers instead of Demon. This new Clan was made specifically to hunt down and kill the True Brujah. True Faith was one of their powers, and cost next to nothing to get for the Elders. After 400 years my character found out about them after a botched assassination attempt at his castle and some torture done by his favorite Ghoul Boris. Boris was 500 years old at this point, had 500 wives, 3000 children, 10000 grand children, 30000 great grand children etc etc.<br /> <br /> Cage then learned that his Sire had broken into the Vatican Library for a book, and accidentally killed the Pope 300 years in the past. Long story short, the group killed the new Pope and brought him back as a zombie, found the Antediluvian, and Cage killed him in a fist fight when he did over 200 damage in a single round of combat, right after killing his 5 Eldest childer at the same time. The rest of the group held back the whole army 1000 of 8-13 gens, and the whole human army while I fought, since they all banked on that I would be the only person able to fight him at all, they didn't have any Fortitude or Potence. Assamite, Tzimisce, and Cappadocians are great at fighting numbers, don't let anyone tell you otherwise. They were trying to find Elios' soul so that they could torture them and use their power. He then diablerized the Antediluvian after punching them so hard that he broke the Antediluvian's plot armor.<br /> <br /> And that's how the Brujah got their Antediluvian back. I also met both Cappadocius and Tremere during their hay day. Tremere was a walking inferno that would instantly vaporize those that didn't have Fortitude, and Cappadocius was insane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T21:50:28-07:00","id":88653,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Jason Shadow-Walker</b></span><br /> <img src=\"https://imageshack.com/a/img923/1335/Q3tzoq.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Weretiger \u2022 Mage \u2022 Super-Twink with maxed stats.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> An Order of Hermes Mage, Jason was an officer of the law. An altercation in the streets happened to reveal several other un-affiliated magi running around, fighting a group of Technocratic agents who were seeking their mortal ends. Jason wound up getting involved with them and starting a cabal with them... almost immediately, things got very odd as the group went deep into a technocracy base to recover a captured master of magick. However, while within the Technocratic prison, they came across others that were captured, including shape-shifters. In a botched (7 ones, no successes) attempt to teleport Jason and a weretiger, the two were merged into one body (not all freaky-looking though) and Jason's Avatar defeated the weretiger's spirit for control. However, because the spirit wasn't destroyed, Jason had control over both his Avatar and the &quot;avatar&quot; of the weretiger, giving him access to both his Magick and to the spiritual and shape-shifting powers of the weretiger.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The group emerged from the base and were lead by their new Master into a war in another world where an evil empire known as the &quot;Sturg Empire&quot; was fighting a rebellion that very much mirrored the Mages and the Technocracy. This &quot;world&quot; was actually more like a fantastic solar system of its own, with other planets, space ships, space stations and odd &quot;stars&quot; with their own strange properties (including the &quot;Time Star&quot; and &quot;Void Star&quot;.) With the aid of the rebels, Jason became augmented with cyberware, allowing him to control a large combat suit through a data port tied directly into his brain. With it he could control computers, pilot spaceships, and access firing controls of large weaponry that he could only use while wearing the suit (or, in Crinos, cuz that was cool too!) However, in a terrible accident, his (new) girlfriend was killed during a fight. Her soul was captured and bound to the computer that Jason carried with him (now a fetish laptop), making it a sentient computer that could act without his needing to command it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> However, even with all of their newfound technology and using their magick, Jason and his allies could not win the war as it was, and so Jason headed off to another world through the &quot;Void Star&quot; where he came across a world that was very open to magick and did not have paradox. It was, however, a strange place where mystical and magical creatures were the norm, and where elves, orcs, and other races lived. He stayed there for some time, building his energies and powers, until he left once more and returned. Even though he had amazing knowledges and understandings of the spheres of magick, Jason still could not defeat the enemies of the rebellion. Eventually he and his group were captured, and in an AMAZING and heroic act, his friend managed to save Jason, his laptop-bound-girlfriend and himself from a diabolical no-win trap and they escaped just as the colossal moon-base exploded. <hr /><br /> <b>In case you hadn't noticed, I am unashamed of the awfulness that is Jason Shadow-Walker. </b>He started as a 1st Edition Mage character in 1994 from my mid-teens and was played for several years in my earliest days of gaming. He's a superb example of a twinkish character that broke all of the rules of the game, in a game that didn't make much sense, but that was <b>a lot of fun to play</b>. I don't try to explain him in any way that makes him sound like he SHOULD exist in any WoD-canon setting, because he's just damned ridiculous. I didn't mention his sleeveless trench coat, his dual-katanas, his BFG Auto-Canon gun, or that other players were playing a vampire and a Mage-Xenomorph shape-shifter either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","user":"Torakhan","date":".  Artwork and formatting 11-07-2018, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T12:37:03-07:00","id":88989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/52935-share-your-signature-character?p=88653#post88653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>In case you hadn't noticed, I am unashamed of the awfulness that is Jason Shadow-Walker.</b></div> </div> </div> </div> Nor should you be! I don't understand how people can appreciate playing regular/Joe Schmoe-power-level games without first having allowed their id to really cut loose at some point on a hyper twink, cross-splat character. This stuff is the cheesecake of cWoD roleplaying. That, and playing/portraying/interacting with any character who <u><i>unironically</i></u> carries around a katana concealed in a trench coat. Delicious.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T17:43:24-07:00","id":89138,"title":"","content":"Jared (Assumed name, Real name lost) - Ravnos - 4th Generation (Originally 13th)<br /> Reborn in the year 1138 in the madness of a giant earthquake in Syria.<br /> Age Unknown, Suffers from Amnesia of his entire human life.<br /> <br /> He has spent over 200 year on every continent. Had dealings with every supernatural creature in the game. Committed diablerie 7 times, the first was on an ancient sabbat vampire whom destroyed the entire crew he was running with at the time. Its blood was so potent his generation dropped drastically and he gained an addiction to vampire blood. When the week of nightmares came to pass he was 8th generation at the beginning and 4th when his founders ash had finished settling, which incidentally also sated his 800+ year blood lust but leaving him barely human with and aura that is completely black.<br /> <br /> His disciplines list is extremely well versed and quite ridiculous honestly, giving him many options when he comes to town which is good because he is on every list that carries a bounty. He travels with a large mixed group of vampires, sorcerers, ghouls, and even normal humans from all around the world which help him stay alive and out of the public eye. He and his group have laid waste to both a Sabbat and Anarch city simply because they got wind that his group was near by.<br /> <br /> In truth, unbeknownst to even his own crew, since the Week of Nightmares ended his body has been in an undisclosed location. Fueled by his mastery of Auspex and Chimestry, every time he has surfaced it has actually been an illusion, or his consciousness imparted into a mortal host via Dominate and his Obfuscate used to conceal the fact it isn't really him. When he makes an appearance with characters he is willing to give them their hearts desire, for a price, and he takes welching on a deal very personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T07:19:19-07:00","id":100714,"title":"","content":"Godfrey Burns<br /> 13th Generation Brujah<br /> <br /> Born Gordon Godfrey Burns jr in New York to an American father and English mother, Gordon joined the CIA and was trained in cyber-operations.<br /> After suffering injuries during a counter-terrorism operation Gordon left the CIA and moved to Los Angeles setting up a driving school, instructing security firms in escape and evasion driving.<br /> It was at this time that he dropped his christian name Gordon in favour of his middle name Godfrey.<br /> <br /> His knowledge of computer security and impressive driving skills caught the eye of an up-and-coming Brujah, Salvatorie Ragonesi, who ghouled Godfrey to be his personal chauffeur and security specialist.<br /> After several years of faithful service, Sal Embraced Godfrey into the Clan.<br /> Godfrey continued to serve his Sire in LA, turning back Sabbat incursions, hunter attacks, defending his Sire\u2019s assets from rivals and becoming embroiled in an ancient prophecy involving pre-Fiat lux entities.<br /> <br /> During a major Sabbat assault on LA in 2005, Godfrey was believed to have met the Final Death whilst buying his Sire and friends time to escape.<br /> In reality he had fallen into Torpor and was rescued by a Brujah Archon.<br /> <br /> Upon awakening a month later Godfrey discovered the small Camarilla court of LA had been completely eradicated, his Sire and allies having declared themselves Anarch.<br /> His devotion and belief in the Camarilla as the only bastion of security in Kindred society, and his extensive understanding of cyber-crime and intelligence gathering led the Camarilla to employ Godfrey as a specialist to counter the ever-increasing threat of tech-savvy Anarchs and Sabbat, grooming him for a new generation of counter-techno-insurgency Archons.<br /> As of tonight everyone he once knew and cared for in LA, including his Sire believe him dead.<br /> <br /> Godfrey gets a brief mention on page 115 of Children of the Revolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T04:22:39-07:00","id":101185,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure my signature Kindred would by my Malkavian Flatter the Hatter<br /> <br /> I was inspired by an AMV of Vampire Bloodlines that featured the male player Malkavian killing/interacting with people to Marilyn Manson's Rock is Dead and a picture of a guy wearing 18th century attire with a wide and wicked smile.<br /> <br /> Anyway the guy is your stereotypical Malkavian that everyone loves to make fun of at least on the surface.<br /> <br /> He is motivated by unearthing kindred lore and seeks to prevent Gehenna however this can prove difficult as he loves to talk in rimes and riddles which he will never drop unless he is extremely angry which isn't often. .<br /> <br /> <br /> He is skilled in sword dueling and carries around a sword cane, but he much rather use his abilities in Demetation. <br /> <br /> <br /> I know he's nothing special but I made him more so for the reactions my fellow players would have both in and out of game when dealing with him.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T16:55:13-07:00","id":101604,"title":"","content":"Maggie (Margaret Mary Carter) 13<sup>th</sup>-&gt;10<sup>th</sup> Gen. Gangrel (translated to Bruja in Requiem)<br /> Embraced: 1969 (Woodstock), at age 30<br /> Sire: Inez (12<sup>th</sup> Gen. Gangrel Antitribu, shortly after \u201creborn\u201d as an Ahrimane)<br /> [My first vampire character back when the game came out in \u201991; played her on-and-off in several different groups during the 90\u2019s and the 00\u2019s.]<br /> Short Overview (her character history is *way* too long to post here, despite only being a vampire for a few decades, so I\u2019m just going to summarize by general years):<br /> <br /> 1939-57: Grew up in northern Virginia, eventually moving to South Carolina; while raised Catholic in her younger years, her teen years were spent adapting to a southern-Baptist lifestyle via her stepfather when her mother remarried after Maggie\u2019s father died in Korea. While not the brightest academically (and not attractive by most standards), Maggie possessed a certain disarming charm and wit that made her socially acceptable enough with other girls (who accepted her as a friend due to her relatively non-threatening-as-a-rival stature) and a \u201cbuddy\u201d-girl for many boys (who saw her as a sort of tomboy who also happened to wear dresses and hang with the \u201cregular\u201d girls). Her attraction, however, to the emerging beat-poet scene \u2013 coupled with a desire to get the fuck out of dodge, as it were\u2013 led her to leaving home without so much as a goodbye after she graduated from high school in \u201957: she took the bitchseat of a passing-by leather-daddy and never looked back\u2026<br /> <br /> 1957-1963: Travelled up and down the East Coast, with cross-country jaunts to California, via several boyfriends. Highs and lows include: meeting Kerouac during a summer jaunt to Florida in \u201957 (and becoming smitten, though he was indifferent to her; he did, however, appreciate her opinion about his just-published \u201cOn the Road\u201d); surviving a motorcycle accident w/a drunken boyfriend; getting a bit too involved with heroin during a New York winter with some wannabe beat-poets; meeting a vampire and a witch in San Francisco, becoming briefly exposed to the supernatural world (though initially writing this off to alcohol and drugs, she later realized that what she had experienced was real when she\u2026).<br /> <br /> 1963, December, California: \u2026is nearly Embraced by a Brujah (Donald) after his newly-created childe (Ronny) almost kills her; Maggie was, however, just alive enough that the blood given her \u201cmerely\u201d ghouled her, and allowed her to recover. She hit the road a few days later, wanting to not think about the incident, though deep down being very intrigued with what she had experienced\u2026<br /> <br /> 1964-1969: Started biking on her own, weaving in-and-out of several biker gangs, and cross-culturing with both folk-groups/performers as well as the nascent hippie movement; in \u201968, meets Bells, a newly made vampire with fantastic insights, though a bit on the flighty-side (Maggie doesn\u2019t realize that Bells is another childe of Donald\u2019s, both because she doesn\u2019t see Donald during the weeks spent with Bells, and because the new vampire doesn\u2019t exhibit any of the traits that the Brujah are known for, being a Caitiff); she travels with Bells and a few other supernaturals on-and-off for almost a year, until arriving \u2013 by accident \u2013 at Woodstock in August of \u201969, where she is ghouled and Embraced over a three night period by Inez, who is creating Maggie as her last childe before being reborn into the Ahrimane bloodline (keeping Maggie a secret from not only her new vampire family, but also keeping Maggie, herself, in the dark about using her as a \u201cmetaphysical anchor\u201d outside of the bloodline \u2013 she leaves Maggie afterwards and to date has never made contact with her again).<br /> <br /> 1970-1990: Maggie adapts very easily to her new existence, traveling with some of the more fringe vampires (Brujah, Malkavians, Caitiff, and even a witch or two linked to Maggie\u2019s loose network of \u201cfriends\u201d), as well as mastering Protean with apparent ease (beginning with the ability to Earth Meld and take on a bestial mein upon awakening after her Embrace, and further developing shape-shifting powers in just a matter of months afterwards); she maintains her casual connection to various biker groups along the East Coast and in California, though more so begins traveling alone across the country to quietly observe different people in different places.<br /> <br /> 1990-1995: Becomes involved with the Sabbat, if only via the Gangrel and Nosferatu Antitribu, spending considerable time in Mexico (learning Spanish, more or less, as well as getting a harsh lesson in exactly how brutal vampires can really be\u2026 She also becomes fairly skilled at Obfuscating, gleaning it from her sometimes-comrades). Upon returning to the U.S., she finds herself embroiled in New York supernatural upheavals, as she makes a tentative acquaintance with a werewolf\u2026<br /> <br /> 1995/96: Having learned some basics about Garou society (at least as far as New York), Maggie embarks on a very dangerous bit of infiltration by posing as a lone werewolf (vouched for, by omission as much as assertion, by her Garou companion, Gil) at several small meetings of other Garou; she is able to successfully pull this off for several months as the meetings are relatively short and those involved are too busy with ongoing supernatural struggles with the Sabbat and Pentex to scrutinize her too closely. She aids her ersatz pack in taking down not only several prominent agents of Pentex, as well as several rival Garou packs, but also preventing the release of a powerful Bane-spirit that would have slowly poisoned/corrupted much of New York City (though, admittedly, even the more mystic \u2013oriented of the werewolves were unsure how to tell if any difference was, in fact, made\u2026). In a climactic battle against a dark-embodied being, Maggie is \u201ckilled\u201d, and her \u201cpackmates\u201d leave it to Gil to treat her as would be appropriate for her upbringing/background; Gil, however, realizes that Maggie is likely not \u201cdead\u201d, as such, as her body doesn\u2019t decay quickly to dust as occurs with most vampires upon final destruction, so he buries her body in Central Park, near the occluded Caern that his pack maintains, leaving her to rest in what he hopes is in peace\u2026<br /> <br /> 2001-05: 5 years later, Maggie was roused from torpor during the week after 9/11: the social turmoil of the mortal world opened up the battlefield for the supernatural underworld, and she found herself quickly involved in Sabbat inter-clan war, along with Camarilla encroachment (the later sect she had never had proper contact with over the previous 3 decades); coupled with werewolves resurging (though her friend Gil was not among them), Maggie found herself taking ardent measures to both survive and gain her bearings in the weeks after rising (she commits diablerie \u2013 something she thought she\u2019d never do \u2013 several times during that year, though mostly in affirmative defense against those seeking to do the same to her; this results in her boosting the power of her blood somewhat, though still not to a degree noticeable enough to discriminate from the power the single-digit generations possess \u2013 to date, Maggie is still very vague about the relative power/concept of \u201cgeneration\u201d, as it applies to vampires, as ironically enough nobody has actually ever really explained the concept to her). She withdraws to Baltimore, Maryland, in 2002, and spends time gathering her wits and infiltrating Ventrue and Sabbat influences in that city. After a few years, she decides to go to California, to see if any of her old comrades are still skulking about there\u2026<br /> <br /> 2005-08: Finding Bells and a few others again, she decides to continue (more earnestly) certain spiritual paths/insights she had loosely flirted with in the 60\u2019s/70\u2019s, attempting to come to a median-balance with her growing vampiric nature. After several years of living mostly in the rural areas of CA (and even being brought into the Umbra several times via her now-aged witch acquaintances), she decides to take \u201cThe Long Sleep\u201d, to see if she can re-spark some dormant aspect of herself, even if only in some small way. She enters torpor on the Autumn Equinox, 2008\u2026<br /> <br /> 2014: Maggie awakens on the Spring Equinox, unsure if anything has changed in any meaningful way, but feeling more centered and secured, almost tranquil, and ready to continue her journey anew\u2026 \u2026until she finds that her witch friends have been murdered during her sleep, and the rural farm-compound where she slept under has been destroyed\u2026<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> (The following stats are using Vampire: Revised, with some homebrewing here and there)<br /> Strength: 3 Charisma: 3 (formerly 4) Perception: 3<br /> Dexterity: 3 Manipulation: 3 Intelligence: 3<br /> Stamina: 2 (-2 pts) Appearance: 1 (Homely, -1) Wits: 4 (Shrewd)<br /> <br /> Talents: Alertness: 3, Athletics: 2, Brawl: 3, Dodge: 3, Empathy: 2 (down 1), Expression: 2 (down 1), Intimidation: 4 (Tough Bitch), Streetwise: 2, Subterfuge: 2 (recently down 1, unknown to her),<br /> Skills: Animal Ken: 2, Drive: 3, Performance: 3, Security: 2, Stealth: 3, Survival: 3<br /> Knowledges: Academics: 1, Investigation: 2, Linguistics: 1, Occult: 2, Werewolf Lore: 1, Sabbat Lore: 1, Mage Lore: 1, Cosmology: 1, Area Knowledge (General Travel, U.S.): 4 (long trips), A.K. (Mexico, General Travel): 2,<br /> <br /> Backgrounds: Arcane: 3 (Maggie doesn\u2019t know that she has this enchantment, placed on her by her recently deceased Allies, to protect her from discovery; the spell was quite strong, and will persist with her possibly as long as she exists, supplementing her other powers of Obfuscate), Contacts:2, Herd: 1, Retainers: 2 (this grouping of backgrounds represents Maggie\u2019s still living human companions in Upstate New York, whom Maggie had ghouled for several years; while the couple are no longer ghouls, their affection for Maggie \u2013 which was legitimately returned by her \u2013 still persists a decade later, so if she can make her way back, she has a haven to recoup and reassess her current situation); all other non-inherent (i.e. excepting Generation, or similar) Backgrounds are currently lost/unavailable,<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Animalism: 3, Fortitude: 4 (bolstered during her diableries in \u201901), Obfuscate: 3, Protean: 5 (mastered very early on, and augmented per below), Potence: 1 (gained during the 90\u2019s after consuming considerable quantities of werewolf blood; Maggie does not actually cognitize that she possesses this minor boost of strength, though she employs it regularly.)<br /> Combos: Co-Inter (Maggie can bring up to 2 additional beings with her when Earth Melding, at 1BP each; she can also, via her Potence variant, \u201cbury\u201d or \u201cexhume\u201d non-living matter/materials via a BP and touching the earth \u2013 or melding down and bringing up such, if the target(s) are more than a couple feet deep); Song of Serenity (during some cross-overs/Ed. Changes, this Animalism power became a special power-option for her as it wasn\u2019t always part of the standard set in a given ST\u2019s game, so I retain it here);<br /> <br /> Conviction: 2 Self-Control: 5 Courage: 4 Path of Honorable Accord: 5* Willpower: 7<br /> *Maggie originally wanted to delve deeper into the precepts of Harmony (even if she didn't understand that, as such), but discovered over the decades that her innate sense of (S)elf (C)ontrol precluded her reaching a certain level of awareness necessary (though said control was very useful, otherwise, in many other situations); under guidance, she eventually adapted the PoHA, though in-character she doesn't identify this &quot;path&quot; in that context -- only as an abstract sense of honor and accordance with others (and, by relation, the world). She will likely advance to 7 in this rather quickly, as it is easier for her to fortify her (C)onviction in it than it was to try to maintain her (C)onscience, particularly given some to the harsh actions she's had to take over the past 20 years or so...<br /> <br /> Merits: <b>Protean Mastery</b> (7pt. addended version: Maggie can assume several tweaked shapes, particularly after her exposure to the Garou during the 90\u2019s: her bat form can vary in size from a standard, small bat to a monstrous looking, very large fruit bat-sized terror; she can assume an appearance approximating that of Glabro (by spending 4 BP to boost Str/Sta to mirror that forms adjustments; in fact, this occurs when she makes these expenditures <i>whether she wants it to or not</i>, as part of her Gangrel weakness), Lupus (by spending an additional 2 BP, above Protean cost, to mirror that forms adj.stats), and Hispo (by spending 5BP above Protean to again simulate adj.stats); <b>Limited Unbondable</b> (2pt.): Maggie is still blood-bound to her sire, so she cannot be blood-bound by others currently; however, the Vaulderie can weaken and possibly break this, per the normal processes, though Maggie has only participated in such a few times, two decades ago, which didn\u2019t result in her bond weakening;<br /> Flaws: <b>Silver Vulnerable</b> (4pt.) \u2013 Maggie doesn\u2019t know that she has this vulnerability, as it only developed after her first torpor, post-werewolf alliance, and she has never been attacked with a silver weapon since then (while she will, of course, be initially surprised at how painful and slow-to-heal such wounds will be, she\u2019ll greet it with a shrug and a \u201cYeah\u2026 that shit *does* kinda\u2019 make sense\u2026\u201d attitude). <b>Prey Exclusion</b>: Mages (2pt.; this \u201cflaw\u201d is one Maggie accepted from her witch companions \u2013 though she doesn\u2019t fully understand how deep in actually runs, nor that she is under a powerful enchantment, as such; Maggie is *incapable* of feeding from any Mage \u2013 and Sorcerers count in this regard \u2013 as their blood/essence simply provides no sustenance for her <i>when not offered of the Mage\u2019s own freewill during a ritual or similar situation, </i>and Maggie will have an instant awareness of a human being a Mage/Sorcerer upon tasting even a drop of their blood; even in the throws of frenzy, she will not seek to feed on such a target, though she may otherwise seek to do them harm per the type of frenzy indicated<b>); Repulsed Invitation</b> (4pt.): Another new limitation \u2013 Maggie must seek admittance to any private domicile (though such admittance *can* be given by any mortal, non-supernatural being within), failure results in her meta-physically *and* physically being unable to enter; while she isn\u2019t harmed, as such, she will find herself physically prevented \u2013 to the point of being physically expelled via the least-resisting exit possible \u2013 from the location; this weakness is peculiar and somewhat mercurial, as even some \u201copen\u201d locations \u2013 such as a well-kept, private garden \u2013 similarly bar her, while the \u201con-paper\u201d owner of a building finds himself unable to repulse her/withdraw permission, as the more spiritual/psychic \u201cowner\u201d is the one more attached ( Ex.: Dad may own the deed in the mundane sense, but *Grandmom* is the one who has lived there since before he was born, and has considerably greater metaphysical investment in the house); once a general invitation is given, she may freely enter afterwards, though the aforementioned \u201cproper owner\u201d may revoke any invitation previously given, resulting in expulsion (If prevented by some greater means from exiting the premises, Maggie suffers a loss of 2 WP and a +2 difficulty on all non-defense rolls, though the penalty doesn\u2019t apply if she is attempting to make an action to free/un-impede herself so as to exit).<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> Was going to post another character (and still may), but good \u2018ol Maggie took up more room than I originally intended (and even some things that could be summarized were *still* left out, let alone the more salient details of her existence), so I\u2019ll post another one later\u2026 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":1433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","user":"Just John, Forever...","date":".  Damn cut 'n paste... 03-29-2014, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T00:53:55-07:00","id":101809,"title":"","content":"I have two that crop up often enough that I could call them &quot;signature characters.&quot;<br /> <br /> The first is a Tzimisce shovelhead embraced in a Camarilla city. He came out of the ground in a fear frenzy (claustrophobia FTW) and fled while the pack that embraced him was trying to corral the other recruits. When he calmed down he tried to go back to his normal life - he worked graveyard at a mortuary - and managed to do so with few hiccups for about two or three years. He ended up meeting his first vampire, a Ventrue that needed to get rid of a body without raising much attention, when said vampire tried to get him to use the crematorium in the basement. He got a crash course in the Camarilla right after that. Everyone just figured he was a Caitiff. He ended up being pretty good as a cleaner and sells his services as such to whoever is willing to pay.<br /> <br /> The second is a Tremere named Baxter Cane. He introduces himself as &quot;Cane. Baxter Cane.&quot; He's a big guy that specializes in Thaumaturgical Countermagic. He's very much not what you expect from your average Tremere (Magic Resistance, Huge Size). He's a security consultant that works closely with the Regent to layer physical and magical security measures. He prefers to spend his time outside of the Chantry because he doesn't feel that he can contribute much to the clan. He is often tasked with tracking down rogue Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/751-dicemauler","name":"dicemauler","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T22:58:55-07:00","id":104624,"title":"","content":"I posted a sketch of my favorite OWoD characters to my art blog today, and figured this would be a good place to <a href=\"http://scottcorpany.tumblr.com/post/81558553202/so-the-mage-the-ascension-20th-anniversary\" target=\"_blank\">share</a>.<br /> <br /> Like a lot of us, I made some characters that were pretty goofy in the early days, but the Brothers Caradoc eventually became a little more refined after a few tearful retcons. There are still some signs of their silly origins though. Three Awakened Hermetic Mages, who are brothers, and sons of a Kinain mother and another Awakened Hermetic Mage father, are far too many supernatural coincidences for one family. Melchior was actually my PC, and the patriarch of the next two generations of PCs, in a series of chronicles that's hit 15 years of real time and is approaching 75 years of game world time. His brothers were major support NPCs before the chronicle moved from Scotland to Seattle, and they were removed more to occasional cameos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T05:15:41-07:00","id":104766,"title":"","content":"Since I have only played Mage the Ascension, because my old RP group mostly despises the dice mechanics for WoD, I only have one iconic character.<br /> <br /> <b>Name</b> - Matthew Burke<br /> <br /> <b>Concept</b> - High school dropout drug addict who awakened to time magic during a trip. Uses his skills and powers as a paranormal investigator.<br /> <br /> A perpetual smirk on his face, with tousled brown hair, stands 5'10&quot;, with a slightly leaner than medium build, stands in a boxer stance. Dresses in casual upscale clothes (black slacks and blue blazers over a white shirt with a tie usually) at his office, and I'm undecided about how he looks when hunting/investigating. Would a trench coat be out of place in this city? What about a fedora?<br /> <br /> His father was an alcoholic wife beater and his mother whored around out of resentment, but made it clear she would never leave him. He used to talk to spirits, at least, until they threatened to have him committed. In his teenage years, Detective Fiction, Noir Fiction and drugs kept him going, although he dropped out of school at sophomore year, and had several Near Death Experiences. The last straw to his failing interest in school and hope for his surroundings was when Men in Black with plasticky faces grabbed his girlfriend, Judy, for <i>questioning</i>, and then she was suddenly never seen again, and no-one would willingly remember even her name when he brought it up. It was like she hadn't existed!!! Dejected, frustrated, more depressed than usual, he struck out from school and his parents' thumb to live at the old city morgue on front street, hustling drugs for money and his own share of the &quot;good stuff&quot;.<br /> <br /> One day, after taking double his usual dose of laudanum laced with cocaine and mescaline, he lay atop an old, long-abandoned slab from the old morgue where he made his home on the streets. He had visions of death, of coming and going, and of the warps and weave in the flow of time itself. He would see someone, fast forward to where their life and his no longer interacted, then jump back to their childhood, and so on ad infinitum, until he could no longer tell what flow of time he was even in. When he woke up, he almost didn't, he felt the need to drift deeper, into a warm sleep that would claim him forever, and had to fight his way to the surface of sleep like a drowning man. After several false awakenings, he finally <b>did </b>awaken, and not only to living (after 3 days of coma-like sleep), but to the flow of time itself. As well, he could see past the veil most people had over their eyes and perceive quintessence, the prime nature of things, bound up into patterns and making up everything around him. He finally <b>knew</b> that there was something weird about this city, and that he had the power to change it, to turn the tides, and thus, set himself up as a paranormal investigator, though he still supplements his income with drugs (possibly gleaned from Dan's character). He successfully gained critical acclaim among paranormal seekers in the area after successfully diagnosing a haunted house , and helping a priest to exorcize it, but is considered a high priced hack among the local law enforcement and mayor and his ilk.<br /> <br /> Preference to Justice with a capital J. Will treat others as they treat him, so will kill a killer and lie to a lier, but not steal from someone who is not a thief. Involves investigating their procedures and habits, like the detective did with the killers in Red Dragon. Ethics are on the questionable side, as he is not above smashing someone's nose to get info or dealing drugs to supplement his income.<br /> <br /> <br /> Treats others mostly as witnesses or suspects, always attempting to glean information and hatch plans of attack. Demeanor is glib and witty. Gestures wildly at times to get his point across, makes good use of his hands for gesturing. Has also studied military signaling for if and when he picks up a partner in investigation.<br /> <br /> Find out what is wrong with the city. Get back his girlfriend. Prove he's worth a damn. Master the flow of time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ally, Cassandra Burnheart, a local assistant DA who has a crush on matt and sometimes pulls official strings for him.<br /> <br /> Contact - Conrad Gester, Curio shop owner and occult scholar, has knowledge of arcane thingamajigs.<br /> Contact - Billy Retton - Local Sheriff, sometimes collaborates with Matt in info gathering although he considers him(Matt) an overpaid hack.<br /> <br /> <b>Spheres \u2013 Time</b>(Primary), <b>Spirit</b>(Secondary)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T07:06:43-08:00","id":1265269,"title":"","content":"Added new-ish artwork for Jason on post #3. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}